    {
      "source": "Doctors of Running",
      "priority": 3,
      "url": "https://www.doctorsofrunning.com/2024/01/nike-alphafly-3-review-2024.html",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: ZoomX is described as soft yet slightly firm under load, with strong heel bounce/impact protection and a more aggressive forefoot push from the Air Zoom pods.",
        "Responsiveness: The ride is repeatedly called aggressive, fast, and highly bouncy, with the stiff/wider plate and forefoot pods giving snappy propulsion at faster paces.",
        "Stability: A wider platform/plate and snug heel provide mild guidance and decent lockdown, but midfoot security can be finicky and some testers found it less confidence-inspiring on turn-heavy courses.",
        "Durability: Durability evidence is limited in this text; it notes an updated outsole and Atomknit built to keep structure, but does not report long-term outsole wear results."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "Road Trail Run",
      "priority": 4,
      "url": "https://www.roadtrailrun.com/2023/12/nike-alphfly-3-review-6-comparisons.html",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: The ride is described as softer and more welcoming than prior Alphaflys, with smoother, less harsh transitions, though the Zoom Air/pod sensation is still very noticeable and can feel mechanical.",
        "Responsiveness: Testers highlight strong midsole energy return and bounce, but some say it is less aggressive/snappy than expected and has less forefoot rebound than Alphafly 1.",
        "Stability: Despite the high stack, reviewers report impressive foot containment, lateral support, and overall stability; the heel counter is lighter and more comfortable, though lockdown depends heavily on the laces due to the tongue-less design.",
        "Durability: Early durability outlook is positive, and outsole grip is praised, but this excerpt provides limited long-term outsole wear/material longevity evidence."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "Believe in the Run",
      "priority": 5,
      "url": "https://believeintherun.com/shoe-reviews/nike-alphafly-3-review/",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: ZoomX with Air Zoom pods is described as soft and protective with a smoother, less mechanical heel-to-forefoot transition; the forefoot feels especially springy and stayed comfortable over marathon distance.",
        "Responsiveness: The ride is repeatedly described as bouncy and propulsive, with freer-moving Air Zoom pods increasing energy return and delivering a snappy toe-off at faster paces.",
        "Stability: Nike added midfoot foam/material to improve stability, the arch is less aggressive, and the Atomknit upper is described as secure/supportive for better lateral control than the prior version.",
        "Durability: The upgraded Fast Shot outsole rubber is called out as tougher, including claims of fewer punctures, indicating improved outsole/material longevity."
      ]
    }
